## 6. Timing Methodology

Timing is an important part of this assignment.

The timer must start:

```text
immediately before the algorithm call
```

and stop:

```text
immediately after the algorithm finishes
```

The following **are NOT** be included:

- File reading.
- Input parsing.
- Memory allocation used as setup.
- Adjacency-list construction.
- CSR conversion.
- Adjacency-matrix construction.
- Result printing.
- File writing.


A valid timing pattern is conceptually:

```text
read input
build data structure
convert to CSR if required

START TIMER
run algorithm
perform algorithm-defined cycle check if applicable
STOP TIMER

print result
print measured time
```

Do not start the timer before input processing or CSR conversion.

