## 8. Performance Notes

### Triangle Counting

Sorting adjacency lists can improve common-neighbour checks and is particularly useful for large graphs.

### Betweenness Centrality

Brandes' algorithm is `O(VE)` for unweighted graphs, so the assignment deliberately uses smaller maximum graph sizes.

### Connected Components

BFS/DFS based connected-component detection is `O(V+E)` and therefore supports the full graph-size scale much more naturally.

